# TPL MMC boot source, layered ON TOP of a -libre defconfig + tpl-spl-chain.config:
#   make libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig tpl-spl-chain.config tpl-mmc.config \
#        olddefconfig
#
# In the chain TPL must fetch SPL from whatever medium the board booted, so the
# SD/eMMC block stack moves INTO the SRAM stage.  That is the opposite of the
# single-stage USB profile, where MMC is pure dead weight -- there the payload
# arrives over the cable and no block device is ever touched.
#
# Cost is the whole point of measuring it: TPL cannot share the SPL phase's
# DM/blk/FDT, it brings its own, so this is not the ~9.8 KB the SPL-side delta
# suggests.  See the size table in
# amlogic/software/boot/gxl/tpl-spl-chain-design.md.

# NOTHING SETS TPL_SIMPLE_BUS HERE, AND THAT IS NOW CORRECT.  mmc@72000 and
# mmc@74000 hang off apb@d0000000, a "simple-bus", and dm_scan_fdt_node() binds
# nothing under a bus that has no driver.  Until 2026-08-12 this fragment could
# therefore never have bound a card -- nobody noticed because no TPL had ever
# read one.  The repair is in drivers/core/Kconfig, where TPL_SIMPLE_BUS now
# carries the same `default y` its SIMPLE_BUS and SPL_SIMPLE_BUS siblings
# always had, so TPL_DM + TPL_OF_CONTROL below is enough to bring it in.
#
# DONE 2026-08-30: `soc { bootph-all; }` marks the BUS, not its children, so
# apb@d0000000 and the two mmc nodes needed their own marks in the board u-boot
# dtsi the way cbus and spifc got theirs.  They now have bootph-pre-sram,
# guarded on TPL_MESON_GX_LOAD_MMC.  Measured: the pruned TPL device tree went
# 811 B (/chosen, /soc, /soc/vpu -- no controller at all) to 2046 B carrying
# apb@d0000000, mmc@72000, mmc@74000 and the mmc0/mmc1 aliases; the TPL binary
# went 42859 -> 44094 B of 45056.

# The block stack.  BLK + DM_MMC is the full path, not MMC_TINY: SPL_MMC_TINY
# has no TPL_ analogue at all (common/spl/Kconfig, "depends on SPL_MMC"), so
# CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(MMC_TINY) is unconditionally false in this phase.
CONFIG_TPL_MMC=y
CONFIG_TPL_DM_MMC=y
CONFIG_TPL_BLK=y
CONFIG_TPL_DM=y
CONFIG_TPL_DM_SEQ_ALIAS=y

# A real device tree, because the MMC controller is described by one.  TPL gets
# its own pruned copy (bootph-* nodes only) appended to the binary; the pair
# still has to fit the 0xb000 amlimage payload ceiling, which is what the
# TPL_MAX_SIZE in spl-usb.config enforces.
CONFIG_TPL_OF_CONTROL=y
CONFIG_TPL_OF_REAL=y
CONFIG_TPL_OF_TRANSLATE=y
CONFIG_TPL_OF_LIBFDT=y

# The board's SD and eMMC controllers.  There is no TPL_MMC_MESON_GX to set:
# drivers/mmc/Makefile is obj-$(CONFIG_MMC_MESON_GX), not phase-gated, so the
# driver comes along as soon as TPL_MMC lets the build descend into drivers/mmc.
#
# NO CLK UCLASS HERE, ON PURPOSE -- and this is the settled answer, not a gap.
#
# The probe used to die before it started: meson_mmc_probe() opens with
# clk_get_bulk(), and with the CLK uclass absent from a phase include/clk.h
# supplies a static inline returning -ENOSYS, which the probe returned
# unchanged, so the loader below refused with GX_TPL_LOAD_NO_DEV.
#
# Turning CLK on was never the fix, only a more expensive failure:
#
#   CONFIG_TPL_CLK=y + CONFIG_TPL_PINCTRL=y
#     -> undefined reference to regmap_read / regmap_update_bits / regmap_write
#        / syscon_node_to_regmap from drivers/clk/meson/gxbb.c.  TPL_REGMAP and
#        TPL_SYSCON are prompt-less bools that nothing selects -- the same shape
#        as the TPL_SPRINTF / TPL_STRTO gap closed in ea618da0a1b, and the same
#        one the design doc records for meson_spifc.
#     -> AND, before any of that could be linked: region '.sram' overflowed by
#        23864 bytes.  The GXBB clock driver does not fit under the 0xb000
#        amlimage ceiling, and 23864 is a LOWER bound -- regmap and syscon are
#        not in that figure because the link never got that far.
#
# Measured on AML-S905X-CC 2026-08-07 with the board sitting in BROM, over
# REQ_READ_MEM/REQ_WRITE_MEM: the ROM leaves the GATES on -- HHI_GCLK_MPEG0
# 0xffffffff (SD_EMMC_A/B/C), HHI_NAND_CLK_CNTL 0x80, HHI_SD_EMMC_CLK_CNTL
# 0x00800080 -- and what is NOT set up is the controller's own SD_EMMC_CLOCK,
# which read 0 while SD_EMMC_CFG faulted.  Writing SD_EMMC_CLOCK directly
# (0x0100023c) and nothing else took SD_EMMC_CFG from a bus fault to
# 0x00004890.  meson_mmc_config_clock() already does exactly that write, with a
# plain meson_write() and no clock framework -- so clk_get_bulk()'s -ENOSYS is
# now non-fatal in the TPL phase (drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c) and TPL_CLK,
# TPL_REGMAP, TPL_SYSCON and the 23864-byte overflow are all avoided by not
# being incurred.
#
# Same reasoning covers TPL_PINCTRL: the ROM muxed these pins to boot.  That
# part is INFERENCE, not measurement -- no run has confirmed a transaction.
# CONFIG_TPL_CLK is not set
# CONFIG_TPL_PINCTRL is not set

# common/spl/Makefile builds spl_mmc.o from CONFIG_$(PHASE_)MMC, and that file
# is written against the generic loader, so TPL_MMC drags the xPL framework in
# whether or not anything calls it.  Set it explicitly rather than letting
# olddefconfig discover it: the cost belongs in the fragment where it can be
# read, and TPL_FRAMEWORK is also what makes spl_early_init() available, which
# is how the loader gets a bound MMC controller.
CONFIG_TPL_FRAMEWORK=y

# Ask TPL to actually use it.
#
# The symbol is TPL_MESON_GX_LOAD_MMC -- phase prefix FIRST, as Kconfig requires
# for a phase-gated symbol -- and that is the spelling arch/arm/mach-meson/Kconfig
# declares, arch/arm/mach-meson/Makefile keys tpl-load-mmc.o on, and spl.c tests
# in three places.  This fragment carried MESON_GX_TPL_LOAD_MMC from the day it
# was written, which names nothing: kconfig SILENTLY DROPS an assignment to an
# undeclared symbol, olddefconfig prints no warning, and the build succeeds.  So
# every MMC-arm size ever recorded for this fragment measured the block stack
# WITHOUT the loader it exists to enable -- tpl-load-mmc.o was never linked, and
# gx_tpl_fetch_spl() would have refused with GX_TPL_LOAD_NO_MMC on real silicon,
# which is exactly the run no board has done yet.
CONFIG_TPL_MESON_GX_LOAD_MMC=y
